title: 'statement-store: persist transient statements and sweep them once propagated'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On nodes running the v2 DHT statement path, a statement no affinity covers is admitted to the
    store like any other and removed by the maintenance sweep once it has been propagated, with the
    usual re-acceptance ban, unless affinity has arrived by then. It was previously held in memory
    and handed out once on the propagation pull. Nodes without the v2 DHT path enabled are
    unaffected.

crates:
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: minor
